From the release policy, we learn that production model changes require an evaluation on a frozen holdout. Promotion is authorized only if the F1 score improves by at least 0.005 and the ROC-AUC does not drop by more than 0.01. A drift alert alone does not justify production changes; there must be additional validation metrics meeting the specified criteria.

A search timeout would likely indicate a problem with the model's performance evaluation process, but it does not directly affect the decision to promote a model based on drift alone. Drift alone is insufficient to justify production changes without meeting the specified performance criteria.

